---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
const lang = 'en';
---
<Layout
  title="Getting physically ready for a motorcycle raid · CDM Motorsport"
  description="Cardio, strength, hydration, recovery: how to prepare physically for a motorcycle rally-raid in Morocco, without overcomplicating things."
  ogImage="/img/gallery/gallery-04.jpg"
  lang={lang}
>
  <section class="phero short" style="background-image:url('/img/gallery/gallery-04.jpg')">
    <div class="wrap c">
      <div class="eyebrow" style="color:#e8c9a6">Advice</div>
      <h1>Physical <em>prep</em></h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pad">
    <div class="wrap article">
      <div class="meta reveal">Advice · 5 min read</div>
      <div class="big reveal" style="margin-bottom:24px">
        Getting physically ready<br />for a <em>motorcycle raid</em>
      </div>
      <div class="reveal">
        <p>
          A raid is several days of effort on terrain that doesn't forgive fatigue. I tell
          everyone who comes along, straight up: a little preparation beforehand changes
          everything, both for the enjoyment and for safety.
        </p>
        <p>
          The most useful thing is cardio. A few weeks of running, cycling or swimming
          before you leave, and you'll hold up a lot better on the long stages, when the
          heat and the kilometers start to weigh. Nothing extreme, just consistency.
        </p>
        <p>
          A bit of strength work doesn't hurt either. On an off-road bike, you're
          constantly working your legs, upper body and, above all, your core. It saves you
          a lot of soreness and cuts down the risk of silly injuries.
        </p>
        <p>
          On the ground, two things make the difference: drink a lot, really a lot in the
          desert, and recover well in the evening. A good night's sleep and a proper meal,
          and you set off fresh the next morning.
        </p>
        <p>
          On the day itself, nothing replaces time in the saddle. You manage your effort,
          you listen to your body, and you enjoy it. I make sure everyone moves at their
          own pace, without ever tipping into the red. <a href="/en/#raids">My raids</a>.
        </p>

        <p style="margin-top:28px">
          Ready to take the plunge?
        </p>
        <a href="/en/reserver" class="btn dark" style="margin-top:14px">Book a raid</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
